IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`

-- ccc14-part122-disclosure.l4 -- PART XII.2 "Proceeds of Crime", ss 462.47 to 462.5 (disclosure provisions; income tax information; specific rules of forfeiture; regulations) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`), `daydate`, and the keel's definitions (`ccc-definitions`) for the one enumeration `s 2 form of the charge`.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: JUST TRUE = the text brings the case within the provision; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered (see NOTES.md).

§ `PART XII.2 -- Proceeds of Crime: disclosure, income tax information, forfeiture rules, regulations (ss 462.47 to 462.5)`

§§ `s 462.47 -- No civil or criminal liability incurred by informants`

-- src:8353 | 462.47 For greater certainty but subject to section 241 of the Income Tax Act, a person is justified in disclosing to a peace officer or the Attorney General any facts on the basis of which that person reasonably suspects that any property is proceeds of crime or that any person has committed or is about to commit a designated offence.
@ref s 462.47 (src:8353)
GIVEN `the person discloses facts to a peace officer or the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facts are the basis on which the person reasonably suspects that any property is proceeds of crime or that any person has committed or is about to commit a designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 241 of the Income Tax Act prevents the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.47 the person is justified in disclosing the facts to a peace officer or the Attorney General` MEANS
    IF `section 241 of the Income Tax Act prevents the disclosure`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to section 241 of the Income Tax Act"
    ELSE IF `the person discloses facts to a peace officer or the Attorney General`
            AND `the facts are the basis on which the person reasonably suspects that any property is proceeds of crime or that any person has committed or is about to commit a designated offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person is justified in disclosing to a peace officer or the Attorney General any facts on the basis of which that person reasonably suspects"

§§ `s 462.48 -- Disclosure of income tax information`

-- src:8355 | 462.48 (1) In this section, designated substance offence means
-- src:8356 | (a) an offence under Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, except subsection 4(1) of that Act;
-- src:8357 | (a.1) an offence under Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act, except subsection 8(1) of that Act; or
-- src:8358 | (b) a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in paragraph (a) or (a.1).
@ref s 462.48(1) "designated substance offence" (src:8355-8358)
GIVEN form IS A `s 2 form of the charge`
      `the offence is under Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under subsection 4(1) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under subsection 8(1) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(1) designated substance offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (form EQUALS `the offence itself` OR form EQUALS `a conspiracy to commit the offence` OR form EQUALS `an attempt to commit the offence`
            OR form EQUALS `being an accessory after the fact in relation to the offence` OR form EQUALS `counselling in relation to the offence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "designated substance offence means"
    ELSE IF (`the offence is under Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` AND NOT `the offence is under subsection 4(1) of that Act`)   -- (a), (b)
            OR (`the offence is under Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act` AND NOT `the offence is under subsection 8(1) of that Act`)   -- (a.1), (b)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offence under Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, except subsection 4(1) of that Act"

-- src:8360 | (1.1) The Attorney General may make an application in accordance with subsection (2) for an order for disclosure of information under subsection (3), for the purposes of an investigation in relation to
-- src:8361 | (a) a designated substance offence;
-- src:8362 | (b) an offence against subsection 119(1), section 120, subsection 121(1) or (2), section 122 or subsection 123(1) or (2), or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence;
-- src:8363 | (b.1) an offence against subsection 279.01(1), 279.011(1) or 279.02(1) or (2) or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence;
-- src:8364 | (b.2) an offence against subsection 346(1) or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence;
-- src:8365 | (b.3) an offence against paragraph 380(1)(a) or subsection 380(2) or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence;
-- src:8366 | (c) an offence against section 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13, or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence;
-- src:8367 | (d) a terrorism offence;
-- src:8368 | (e) an offence against subsection 3(1) of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence; or
-- src:8369 | (f) an offence against section 354, 355.2, 355.4 or 462.31 — or a conspiracy or attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to such an offence — if the offence is alleged to have been committed in relation to any property, thing or proceeds obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of
-- src:8370 | (i) the commission in Canada of an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e), or
-- src:8371 | (ii) an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence referred to in any of those paragraphs.
@ref s 462.48(1.1) (src:8360-8371)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      form IS A `s 2 form of the charge`
      `the offence is a designated substance offence, by s 462.48(1) designated substance offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is under subsection 3(1) of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, or is a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is alleged to have been committed in relation to any property, thing or proceeds obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e), or of an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(1.1) the Attorney General may apply for an order for disclosure of information for the purposes of an investigation in relation to the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is a designated substance offence, by s 462.48(1) designated substance offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        OR `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
        OR `the offence is under subsection 3(1) of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act, or is a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to, such an offence`   -- (e)
        OR (`the form of the charge is one the paragraphs name` AND (`the section is one that paragraphs (b) to (c) name` OR (`the section is one that paragraph (f) names` AND `the offence is alleged to have been committed in relation to any property, thing or proceeds obtained or derived directly or indirectly as a result of an offence referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e), or of an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted such an offence`)))   -- (b) to (c), (f)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purposes of an investigation in relation to"
    WHERE
        -- "or a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, or being an accessory after the fact in relation to": counselling is not named in paragraphs (b) to (f)
        `the form of the charge is one the paragraphs name` MEANS
            form EQUALS `the offence itself` OR form EQUALS `a conspiracy to commit the offence` OR form EQUALS `an attempt to commit the offence` OR form EQUALS `being an accessory after the fact in relation to the offence`
        `the section is one that paragraphs (b) to (c) name` MEANS
            (provision's `section` EQUALS 119 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")   -- (b)
            OR provision's `section` EQUALS 120
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 121 AND (provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR provision's `section` EQUALS 122
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 123 AND (provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 279.01 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")   -- (b.1)
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 279.011 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 279.02 AND (provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 346 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")   -- (b.2)
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 380 AND (provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(1)(a)" OR provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))   -- (b.3)
            OR provision's `section` EQUALS 52 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 52.1 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 52.2   -- (c)
            OR provision's `section` EQUALS 467.11 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 467.111 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 467.12 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 467.13
        `the section is one that paragraph (f) names` MEANS
            provision's `section` EQUALS 354 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 355.2 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 355.4 OR provision's `section` EQUALS 462.31

-- src:8373 | (2) An application under subsection (1.1) shall be made ex parte in writing to a judge and be accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or a person specially designated by the Attorney General for that purpose deposing to the following matters, namely,
-- src:8374 | (a) the offence or matter under investigation;
-- src:8375 | (b) the person in relation to whom the information or documents referred to in paragraph (c) are required;
-- src:8376 | (c) the type of information or book, record, writing, return or other document obtained by or on behalf of the Minister of National Revenue for the purposes of Part IX of the Excise Tax Act, the Income Tax Act, the Excise Act, 2001, the Underused Housing Tax Act, the Select Luxury Items Tax Act or the Global Minimum Tax Act to which access is sought or that is proposed to be examined or communicated; and
-- src:8377 | (d) the facts relied on to justify the belief, on reasonable grounds, that the person referred to in paragraph (b) has committed or benefited from the commission of any of the offences referred to in subsection (1.1) and that the information or documents referred to in paragraph (c) are likely to be of substantial value, whether alone or together with other material, to the investigation for the purposes of which the application is made.
@ref s 462.48(2) (src:8373-8377)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte in writing to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or a person specially designated by the Attorney General for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the offence or matter under investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the person in relation to whom the information or documents are required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the type of information or book, record, writing, return or other document obtained by or on behalf of the Minister of National Revenue to which access is sought or that is proposed to be examined or communicated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the facts relied on to justify the belief, on reasonable grounds, that the person has committed or benefited from the commission of any of the offences referred to in subsection (1.1) and that the information or documents are likely to be of substantial value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(2) the application complies with subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte in writing to a judge`
        AND `the application is accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or a person specially designated by the Attorney General for that purpose`
        AND `the affidavit deposes to the offence or matter under investigation`   -- (a)
        AND `the affidavit deposes to the person in relation to whom the information or documents are required`   -- (b)
        AND `the affidavit deposes to the type of information or book, record, writing, return or other document obtained by or on behalf of the Minister of National Revenue to which access is sought or that is proposed to be examined or communicated`   -- (c)
        AND `the affidavit deposes to the facts relied on to justify the belief, on reasonable grounds, that the person has committed or benefited from the commission of any of the offences referred to in subsection (1.1) and that the information or documents are likely to be of substantial value`   -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under subsection (1.1) shall be made ex parte in writing to a judge and be accompanied by an affidavit"

-- src:8379 | (3) Where the judge to whom an application under subsection (1.1) is made is satisfied
-- src:8380 | (a) of the matters referred to in paragraph (2)(d), and
-- src:8381 | (b) that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access to the information or documents to which the application relates, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation if the access is obtained,
-- src:8382 | the judge may, subject to any conditions that the judge considers advisable in the public interest, order the Commissioner of Revenue or any person specially designated in writing by the Commissioner for the purposes of this section
-- src:8383 | (c) to allow a police officer named in the order access to all such information and documents and to examine them, or
-- src:8384 | (d) where the judge considers it necessary in the circumstances, to produce all such information and documents to the police officer and allow the police officer to remove the information and documents,
-- src:8385 | within such period after the expiration of seven clear days following the service of the order pursuant to subsection (4) as the judge may specify.
@ref s 462.48(3) (src:8379-8385)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied of the matters referred to in paragraph (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access to the information or documents to which the application relates, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation if the access is obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(3) the judge may order the Commissioner of Revenue to allow a police officer named in the order access to the information and documents and to examine them` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied of the matters referred to in paragraph (2)(d)` AND `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access to the information or documents to which the application relates, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation if the access is obtained`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (c)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the judge to whom an application under subsection (1.1) is made is satisfied"

@ref s 462.48(3)(d) (src:8384)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied of the matters referred to in paragraph (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access to the information or documents to which the application relates, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation if the access is obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers it necessary in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(3)(d) the judge may order the production of the information and documents to the police officer and allow the police officer to remove them` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied of the matters referred to in paragraph (2)(d)` AND `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for believing that it is in the public interest to allow access to the information or documents to which the application relates, having regard to the benefit likely to accrue to the investigation if the access is obtained` AND `the judge considers it necessary in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the judge considers it necessary in the circumstances"

-- "within such period after the expiration of seven clear days following the service of the order": the caller states the number of clear days that have passed (the text does not define "clear days"; see NOTES.md, fork register).
@ref s 462.48(3) (src:8385)
GIVEN `the number of clear days that have passed since the service of the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(3) the period for compliance with the order has begun` MEANS
    IF `the number of clear days that have passed since the service of the order` AT LEAST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within such period after the expiration of seven clear days following the service of the order"

-- src:8387 | (4) A copy of an order made by a judge under subsection (3) shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court.
@ref s 462.48(4) (src:8387)
GIVEN `a copy of the order was served on the person to whom the order is addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was served in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(4) the order has been served as subsection (4) requires` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the order was served on the person to whom the order is addressed` AND `it was served in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court"

-- src:8389 | (5) A judge who makes an order under subsection (3) may, on application of the Minister of National Revenue, extend the period within which the order is to be complied with.
@ref s 462.48(5) (src:8389)
GIVEN `the judge made an order under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application to extend the period is made by the Minister of National Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(5) the judge may extend the period within which the order is to be complied with` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application to extend the period is made by the Minister of National Revenue`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the Minister of National Revenue" (a gate of the kind "on application" on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the judge made an order under subsection (3)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge who makes an order under subsection (3)"

DECLARE `s 462.48(6) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.48(6)(a) the Minister of National Revenue is prohibited from disclosing the information or document by any bilateral or international treaty, convention or other agreement respecting taxation to which the Government of Canada is a signatory`
    `s 462.48(6)(b) a privilege is attached by law to the information or document`
    `s 462.48(6)(c) the information or document has been placed in a sealed package pursuant to law or an order of a court of competent jurisdiction`
    `s 462.48(6)(d) disclosure of the information or document would not, for any other reason, be in the public interest`
    `s 462.48(6) a ground that is none of those`

-- src:8391 | (6) The Minister of National Revenue or any person specially designated in writing by that Minister for the purposes of this section may object to the disclosure of any information or document in respect of which an order under subsection (3) has been made by certifying orally or in writing that the information or document should not be disclosed on the ground that
-- src:8392 | (a) the Minister of National Revenue is prohibited from disclosing the information or document by any bilateral or international treaty, convention or other agreement respecting taxation to which the Government of Canada is a signatory;
-- src:8393 | (b) a privilege is attached by law to the information or document;
-- src:8394 | (c) the information or document has been placed in a sealed package pursuant to law or an order of a court of competent jurisdiction; or
-- src:8395 | (d) disclosure of the information or document would not, for any other reason, be in the public interest.
@ref s 462.48(6) (src:8391-8395)
GIVEN `the person objecting is the Minister of National Revenue or a person specially designated in writing by that Minister for the purposes of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 462.48(6) ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(6) the person may object to the disclosure on the ground` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person objecting is the Minister of National Revenue or a person specially designated in writing by that Minister for the purposes of this section`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Minister of National Revenue or any person specially designated in writing by that Minister for the purposes of this section may object"
    ELSE CONSIDER ground
         WHEN `s 462.48(6) a ground that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8397 | (7) Where an objection to the disclosure of information or a document is made under subsection (6), the objection may be determined, on application, in accordance with subsection (8), by the Chief Justice of the Federal Court, or by such other judge of that Court as the Chief Justice may designate to hear such applications.
@ref s 462.48(7) (src:8397)
GIVEN `an objection to the disclosure of information or a document is made under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person determining it is the Chief Justice of the Federal Court, or such other judge of that Court as the Chief Justice may designate to hear such applications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(7) the objection may be determined, on application, by the Chief Justice of the Federal Court or a judge the Chief Justice designates` MEANS
    IF NOT `an objection to the disclosure of information or a document is made under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an objection to the disclosure of information or a document is made under subsection (6)" (a "where" gate on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the person determining it is the Chief Justice of the Federal Court, or such other judge of that Court as the Chief Justice may designate to hear such applications`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by the Chief Justice of the Federal Court, or by such other judge of that Court as the Chief Justice may designate to hear such applications"

-- src:8399 | (8) A judge who is to determine an objection pursuant to subsection (7) may, if the judge considers it necessary to determine the objection, examine the information or document in relation to which the objection is made and shall grant the objection and order that disclosure of the information or document be refused where the judge is satisfied of any of the grounds mentioned in subsection (6).
@ref s 462.48(8) (src:8399)
GIVEN `the judge considers it necessary to determine the objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(8) the judge may examine the information or document` MEANS
    IF `the judge considers it necessary to determine the objection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, if the judge considers it necessary to determine the objection, examine the information or document"

@ref s 462.48(8) (src:8399)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied of any of the grounds mentioned in subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(8) the judge must grant the objection and order that disclosure of the information or document be refused` MEANS
    IF `the judge is satisfied of any of the grounds mentioned in subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the judge is satisfied of any of the grounds mentioned in subsection (6)"

-- src:8401 | (9) An application under subsection (7) shall be made within ten days after the objection is made or within such greater or lesser period as the Chief Justice of the Federal Court, or such other judge of that Court as the Chief Justice may designate to hear such applications, considers appropriate.
@ref s 462.48(9) (src:8401)
GIVEN `the date the objection is made` IS A DATE
      `the date the application under subsection (7) is made` IS A DATE
      `the number of days of the period the Chief Justice or the designated judge considers appropriate, or 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(9) the application is made in time` MEANS
    IF `the number of days of the period the Chief Justice or the designated judge considers appropriate, or 0 if none` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN (IF `the date the application under subsection (7) is made` AT MOST Date (Day `the date the objection is made` PLUS `the number of days of the period the Chief Justice or the designated judge considers appropriate, or 0 if none`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within such greater or lesser period as the Chief Justice of the Federal Court, or such other judge of that Court as the Chief Justice may designate to hear such applications, considers appropriate"
    ELSE (IF `the date the application under subsection (7) is made` AT MOST Date (Day `the date the objection is made` PLUS 10)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within ten days after the objection is made"

-- src:8403 | (10) An appeal lies from a determination under subsection (7) to the Federal Court of Appeal.
@ref s 462.48(10) (src:8403)
GIVEN `the appeal is from a determination under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(10) an appeal lies to the Federal Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is from a determination under subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal lies from a determination under subsection (7) to the Federal Court of Appeal"

-- src:8405 | (11) An appeal under subsection (10) shall be brought within ten days from the date of the determination appealed from or within such further time as the Federal Court of Appeal considers appropriate in the circumstances.
@ref s 462.48(11) (src:8405)
GIVEN `the date of the determination appealed from` IS A DATE
      `the date the appeal is brought` IS A DATE
      `the number of days of the further time the Federal Court of Appeal considers appropriate, or 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(11) the appeal is brought in time` MEANS
    IF `the number of days of the further time the Federal Court of Appeal considers appropriate, or 0 if none` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN (IF `the date the appeal is brought` AT MOST Date (Day `the date of the determination appealed from` PLUS `the number of days of the further time the Federal Court of Appeal considers appropriate, or 0 if none`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or within such further time as the Federal Court of Appeal considers appropriate in the circumstances"
    ELSE (IF `the date the appeal is brought` AT MOST Date (Day `the date of the determination appealed from` PLUS 10)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within ten days from the date of the determination appealed from"

-- src:8407 | (12) An application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application shall
-- src:8408 | (a) be heard in camera; and
-- src:8409 | (b) on the request of the person objecting to the disclosure of information, be heard and determined in the National Capital Region described in the schedule to the National Capital Act.
@ref s 462.48(12) (src:8407-8409)
GIVEN `the proceeding is an application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(12)(a) the proceeding must be heard in camera` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is an application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application shall"

@ref s 462.48(12)(b) (src:8409)
GIVEN `the proceeding is an application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person objecting to the disclosure of information requests that it be heard and determined in the National Capital Region described in the schedule to the National Capital Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(12)(b) the proceeding must be heard and determined in the National Capital Region` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is an application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application` AND `the person objecting to the disclosure of information requests that it be heard and determined in the National Capital Region described in the schedule to the National Capital Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the request of the person objecting to the disclosure of information, be heard and determined in the National Capital Region"

-- src:8411 | (13) During the hearing of an application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application, the person who made the objection in respect of which the application was made or the appeal was brought shall, on the request of that person, be given the opportunity to make representations ex parte.
@ref s 462.48(13) (src:8411)
GIVEN `the proceeding is the hearing of an application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who made the objection requests the opportunity to make representations ex parte` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(13) the person who made the objection must be given the opportunity to make representations ex parte` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is the hearing of an application under subsection (7) or an appeal brought in respect of that application` AND `the person who made the objection requests the opportunity to make representations ex parte`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, on the request of that person, be given the opportunity to make representations ex parte"

-- src:8413 | (14) When any information or document is examined or provided under subsection (3), the person by whom it is examined or to whom it is provided or any officer of the Canada Revenue Agency may make, or cause to be made, one or more copies of it, and any copy purporting to be certified by the Minister of National Revenue or an authorized person to be a copy made under this subsection is evidence of the nature and content of the original information or document and has the same probative force as the original information or document would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way.
@ref s 462.48(14) (src:8413)
GIVEN `any information or document is examined or provided under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asking is the person by whom it is examined or to whom it is provided, or an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(14) the person may make, or cause to be made, copies of the information or document` MEANS
    IF NOT `any information or document is examined or provided under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When any information or document is examined or provided under subsection (3)" (a "when" gate on a power, counted with "where" by ruling (c) of 2026-11-05: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the person asking is the person by whom it is examined or to whom it is provided, or an officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person by whom it is examined or to whom it is provided or any officer of the Canada Revenue Agency"

@ref s 462.48(14) (src:8413)
GIVEN `the copy purports to be certified by the Minister of National Revenue or an authorized person to be a copy made under subsection (14)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(14) the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original and has the same probative force` MEANS
    IF `the copy purports to be certified by the Minister of National Revenue or an authorized person to be a copy made under subsection (14)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any copy purporting to be certified by the Minister of National Revenue or an authorized person to be a copy made under this subsection is evidence"

-- src:8415 | (15) No person to whom information or documents have been disclosed or provided pursuant to this subsection or pursuant to an order made under subsection (3) shall further disclose the information or documents except for the purposes of the investigation in relation to which the order was made.
@ref s 462.48(15) (src:8415)
GIVEN `the information or documents have been disclosed or provided to the person pursuant to this subsection or pursuant to an order made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further disclosure is for the purposes of the investigation in relation to which the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(15) the person is barred from further disclosing the information or documents` MEANS
    IF NOT `the information or documents have been disclosed or provided to the person pursuant to this subsection or pursuant to an order made under subsection (3)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person to whom information or documents have been disclosed or provided pursuant to this subsection or pursuant to an order made under subsection (3)"
    ELSE IF `the further disclosure is for the purposes of the investigation in relation to which the order was made`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purposes of the investigation in relation to which the order was made"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The prohibition of subsection (15) as a regulative rule: a person to whom the information was disclosed SHANT further disclose it. The core's Party has no constructor for "any person", so a type of this module's own is declared (NEEDS-CORE.md).
DECLARE `s 462.48 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.48 a person to whom information or documents have been disclosed or provided pursuant to subsection (15) or an order made under subsection (3)`

DECLARE `s 462.48(15) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.48(15) further disclose the information or documents otherwise than for the purposes of the investigation`

@ref s 462.48(15) (src:8415)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 462.48 party` `s 462.48(15) act`
`s 462.48(15) the prohibition on further disclosure` MEANS
    PARTY `s 462.48 a person to whom information or documents have been disclosed or provided pursuant to subsection (15) or an order made under subsection (3)`
    SHANT `s 462.48(15) further disclose the information or documents otherwise than for the purposes of the investigation`
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the information or documents were disclosed further than for the purposes of the investigation in relation to which the order was made"

