GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.48(17) police officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "police officer means any officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace"

§§ `s 462.49 -- Specific rules of forfeiture`

-- src:8423 | 462.49 (1) This Part does not affect the operation of any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting the forfeiture of property.
@ref s 462.49(1) (src:8423)
GIVEN `the other provision respects the forfeiture of property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.49(1) this Part affects the operation of the other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament` MEANS
    IF `the other provision respects the forfeiture of property`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part does not affect the operation of any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting the forfeiture of property"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting the forfeiture of property"

-- src:8425 | (2) The property of an offender may be used to satisfy the operation of a provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting the forfeiture of property only to the extent that it is not required to satisfy the operation of any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting restitution to or compensation of persons affected by the commission of offences.
@ref s 462.49(2) (src:8425)
GIVEN `the value of the property of the offender` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of that property that is required to satisfy the operation of any other provision respecting restitution to or compensation of persons affected by the commission of offences` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 462.49(2) the extent to which the property of the offender may be used to satisfy the operation of a provision respecting the forfeiture of property` MEANS
    IF `the value of the property of the offender` GREATER THAN `the amount of that property that is required to satisfy the operation of any other provision respecting restitution to or compensation of persons affected by the commission of offences`
    THEN `the value of the property of the offender` MINUS `the amount of that property that is required to satisfy the operation of any other provision respecting restitution to or compensation of persons affected by the commission of offences`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 462.5 -- Regulations`

-- src:8429 | 462.5 The Attorney General may make regulations governing the manner of disposing of or otherwise dealing with, in accordance with the law, property forfeited under this Part.
@ref s 462.5, regulation-making power, as the text shows it (src:8429)
`s 462.5 the regulation-making power, as the text shows it` MEANS "The Attorney General may make regulations governing the manner of disposing of or otherwise dealing with, in accordance with the law, property forfeited under this Part."
